<title>SWEDEN: Astra jumps on resignation rumour.</title>
<headline>Astra jumps on resignation rumour.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swedish pharmaceutical concern Astra rose sharply on Tuesday on market rumours that Chief Executive Hakon Mogren was set to resign.</p>
<p>An Astra spokesman immediately dismissed the rumour as baseless. &quot;It seems to be a widespread rumour but that's what's driving the share. I believe it's baseless,&quot; spokesman Staffan Ternby told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;This is childish. There are no grounds for this speculation. Astra's share was quoted at 285.50 crowns at 1220 GMT after opening on Tuesday at 280. Volume was heavy with shares worth 800 million crowns changing hands.&quot;</p>
</text>
